          "merged_at": "2026-09-02T15:40:57Z"
        },
        "body": "## What broke\n\nA scheduler start could resolve the relative `sessions/` directory from a different working directory than manual session tooling. That makes valid `playwright/sessions/bot-X.json` files effectively invisible without deleting them. The workers then fall into interactive login together.\n\nSeparately, a repeated authentication-form stall was being promoted to `VintedSessionBlockedException` even without explicit block-page evidence, so multiple ordinary login stalls appeared in Runtime as `SESSION BLOCKED`.\n\n## Fix\n\n- resolve the default session directory from the Playwright module instead of raw process cwd\n- support an explicit `FLIPBOT_SESSION_DIR` override\n- discover the same module path from repo root, module root, or nested target/classes working directories\n- log the absolute session directory once at startup for immediate diagnostics\n- keep the non-destructive session backup behavior from #130\n- stop promoting generic authentication stalls to `SESSION_BLOCKED`\n- retain late explicit block-page polling, so real Vinted block evidence still uses the persisted session cooldown\n\n## Regression coverage\n\n- repository-root session path resolution\n- module-root session path resolution\n- nested target/classes resolution\n- explicit session-directory override\n- active session remains byte-for-byte intact during recovery\n- repeated auth stalls remain generic failures rather than false session blocks",
